From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Zehnder <markus.z@unfoldedcircle.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [WPE] Key values for ChannelUp, ChannelDown, MediaPlayPause
 and Exit

KeyboardEvent.key and keyCode are derived from the keysym alone, and
four keys of remote controls get no key value of their own:

- KEY_CHANNELUP and KEY_CHANNELDOWN produce the keysyms XF86ChannelUp
  and XF86ChannelDown (0x10081192 and 0x10081193, _EVDEVK() in
  XF86keysym.h, XKB_KEY_XF86ChannelUp/Down in xkbcommon). WPEKeysyms.h
  lacks them because update-keysyms-header skips the _EVDEVK()
  keysyms, so key is "Unidentified" and keyCode 0.
- KEY_PLAYPAUSE and KEY_EXIT have no keysyms of their own: the evdev
  keymap of xkeyboard-config gives them those of KEY_PLAY
  (XF86AudioPlay) and KEY_CLOSE (XF86Close), so key is "MediaPlay" and
  "Close".

Map the two channel keysyms to "ChannelUp" and "ChannelDown" with the
TV key codes VK_CHANNEL_UP (0x1AB) and VK_CHANNEL_DOWN (0x1AC), next to
the DASE/OCAP/CE-HTML codes the colour keys already use. Tell
KEY_PLAYPAUSE and KEY_EXIT apart by the hardware keycode (evdev code
+ 8, as keyCodeStringForWPEKeycode() reads it): XF86AudioPlay on keycode
0xAC is "MediaPlayPause" with VK_MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE, XF86Close on keycode
0xB6 is "Exit"; with any other keycode they stay "MediaPlay" and
"Close". keyValueStringForWPEKeyval() and windowsKeyCodeForWPEKeyval()
take the keycode for this.

Also map two keysyms an XKB keymap produces that had no key value, as
Chromium and Firefox do: ISO_Left_Tab (Shift+Tab) to "Tab", and
XF86Reload (KEY_REFRESH in xkeyboard-config) to "BrowserRefresh" with
VK_BROWSER_REFRESH.

KeyboardEvent.code does not change: the UI Events code specification
has no values for the channel, exit and colour keys, so they stay
"Unidentified".

Upstream: not submitted yet, meant for https://bugs.webkit.org (WPE WebKit)
Signed-off-by: Markus Zehnder <markus.z@unfoldedcircle.com>
